{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPreArchHeatDepthOneKernel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPreArchHeatDepthOneKernel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heat_two_mode_composition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heat_two_mode_composition","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaPreArchHeatDepthOneKernel.lean#L93-L110","doc":"**Heat-mode specialization.** The two-mode composition with the concrete\nper-mode heat kernels `A t = 1 - (q-1)·(μ₁·t)`, `B t = 1 - (q-1)·(μ₂·t)`\n(content-Casimir eigenvalues `μ₁ = μ_λ`, `μ₂ = μ_λ'`): the rank-2 truncation\nof the heat trace `Z_q` satisfies an explicit depth-2 q-difference relation\nwhose coefficients are polynomials in `q`, `μ₁`, `μ₂`, `t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.two_mode_depth_two_composition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.two_mode_depth_two_composition","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaPreArchHeatDepthOneKernel.lean#L69-L91","doc":"**Division-free two-mode composition (depth 2).** If `F`, `G` satisfy\ndepth-1 equations with kernels `A`, `B`, their sum `S = F + G` satisfies the\nexplicit depth-2 relation\n\n  `(B t - A t)·(S (q²t) - A (qt)·S (qt)) = (B (qt) - A (qt))·B t·(S (qt) - A t·S t)`.\n\nThis is the assembly step from per-mode kernels toward heat-trace kernels\n`∏_λ (1 - (q-1)·μ_λ·t)`: no division by the Casoratian is needed, so the\nidentity holds over any commutative ring — fully fibre-level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.heat_mode_depth_one_kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.heat_mode_depth_one_kernel","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaPreArchHeatDepthOneKernel.lean#L55-L67","doc":"**Per-mode heat kernel: depth-1 with kernel `1 - (q-1)·μ·t`.** If `f`\nsatisfies the depth-1 shift equation (e.g. `f = exp_q`), then the heat mode\n`t ↦ f (-(μ·t))` — `μ` a content-Casimir eigenvalue `μ_λ(q)` — satisfies\nthe depth-1 equation whose kernel `1 - (q-1)·μ·t` has its zero located by\nthe spectrum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jackson_fixed_shift_kernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jackson_fixed_shift_kernel","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaPreArchHeatDepthOneKernel.lean#L43-L53","doc":"**The Jackson fixed-point equation is a depth-1 q-difference equation.**\nDenominator-free form of `D_q f = f`: if `f (q·x) - f x = (q-1)·x·f x`\n(the Jackson derivative equation cleared of its `(q-1)·x` denominator),\nthen `f` satisfies the depth-1 shift equation with kernel `1 + (q-1)·x`.\nThis is the pre-archimedean form of the q-exponential's defining equation —\nthe prototype cyclotomic kernel. ","signatureChunk":0}]}